{
  "scope": "One physical iPhone 14 Pro, portrait, one signed isolated fixture binary. Each run is a fresh process; the two start modes alternate (D I I D D I, then I D D I I D). \"deferred\" queues the reader's body read as an ordinary main-actor task; \"immediate\" starts it with Task.immediate when the conversation arrives. Readable means OCR finds section one and another section in a recorded frame. The evicted case rebuilds parsed text from retained HTML. No provider latency is included.",
  "result": "Starting the read immediately moved a prepared disk-backed body's first readable frame from 145.4 to 90.9 ms median after finger lift. For an evicted body the rebuild overlapped the screen transition and took about 94 ms instead of 50 ms, so the opening time did not change materially (161.8 vs 155.1 ms median). Production now starts the read immediately.",
